@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ai-work-shows-from-the-tap
Anything that starts AI work shows its running work log, its first line and its clock, in
the same frame as the tap, before the server answers. A page that tap opens never shows
its "nothing yet" state first ("I feel very lied to", rule 121; J28, J31).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ai-nothing-between-states
When AI work ends the page goes straight from the work log to what the work made, and
from one pass to the next pass's log; no empty or start page shows between (rule 122;
J34).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] ai-work-looks-alive
AI work in progress is always a live, animated indicator, never a blank or a spinner. No
grey skeleton bars sit under it: Tavi called the bars under Ask's steps "awful" and took them
out, so the answer simply arrives where it goes (recording 15 Oct 15:37, 16:24 to 16:37;
L33; this replaces the hint bars of rule 71).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] ai-thinking-line
While work runs there is one shimmering line, a present-tense verb and the elapsed seconds
("Working 12s"); when it ends the line becomes "Worked for 2m 3s" with a chevron that
opens the steps. The internal tool is never named (rules 18 and 72).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] ai-steps-read-calmly
Each step is one plain sentence in regular weight after the icon of what it does, the
icon centred on its line of text. Only a failed step is red: a finished step ("Wrote the
answer") is never red, and no step ("Started") is greyer than the rest. One thing happens
at a time, and there is no "Wrote 3 of 6 stops, Active 3s ago, 4s elapsed" row
(rule 72; recording 15 Oct 13:54, 05:59 to 06:41; K13).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ai-no-machinery-on-content
A tour, a note or an answer does not show the model name, token counts or cache numbers,
and the work log does not start "Started Claude (model id)"; those live in Settings and
the model sheet. Rewrite is an icon at the card's corner with no word (rule 98; F58).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ai-mentions-are-links
Every mention of a file, line, symbol or dimension in a note, the summary, a finding, a
tour or an answer is a link that scrolls to that place, including file names listed in a
code block ("Super, super, super important", rule 96; F43; recording 14 Oct 19:19,
03:43 to 03:55).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ai-names-find-their-files
The app finds the code names the AI did not link: inline code or a word in code's shape
(`PrTourScreen`, `PrTourScreen.kt`, `ReviewScreen.kt:91`, `openAsk`) that is a changed
file's name without its extension is a link that opens that file, in the Tour, Ask and
the summary. A name two files share, and a plain word, stay words (recording of 16 Oct
12:10, 09:25 to 09:47, N17).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] ai-links-look-alike
Links in AI text are teal text with no underline, all in one face: one cite is never in
the code font while the next is not. They sit on the text line and never grow it (rules
39 and 96; F40; recording 15 Oct 13:54, 07:36 to 07:44; K16).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ai-links-read-from-the-root
A link in AI text is read from the repository root: `./` and `../` never go above it, and
a dot-folder (`.agents`, `.github`) keeps its dot. A file the pull request changes opens
in the app's diff; any other opens in the app too, read at the head commit in the same
code view, and a link in AI text MUST NOT open GitHub. Tavi changed this from "any other
opens on GitHub" ("In the code rows still open GitHub", recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 10:01
to 10:07, N20; rule 124; J36).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ai-code-works-like-the-diff
A code block in a tour or an answer is the diff's code view: syntax colours, sideways
scroll and pinch zoom, and a copy button at its top corner that shows the copied toast, as
on a web code block (recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 09:51 to 09:55, N18). Inline code shows as
code and never with its backticks (rule 95; F59, F63).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ai-structures-are-drawn
A flow, a call tree and a file tree are drawn by the app from structured data, never
printed as text; a flow line that does not parse stays as words in its place. A file in a
tree that the pull request changes opens it (rule 95; F59; recording 14 Oct 19:19, 04:01).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] ai-flow-is-steps-on-a-rail
A flow is numbered steps on a rail: each part a card the width of the block with its
number in a dot on the rail, each hop the rail with an arrowhead down to the next dot and
what moves beside it ("the Flow block needs visual work", recording of 16 Oct 12:10,
09:56 to 09:58, N19).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] ai-call-tree-reads-at-a-glance
A call tree sits in a well like code, its names in the code face on guide lines that end
in a dot at each row. A call written as a chain puts each step on a line of its own, its
arrow in one column under the name, so the steps line up and never wrap into each other
("really easy and nice to look at", recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 09:17 to 09:24, N16).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] ai-sketch-label-is-one-paragraph
A sketch's or a diagram's kind and its caption are one paragraph above it, the caption
wrapping under the kind from the left edge, and the caption is one short sentence; the
brief's prompt asks the model for one (recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 17:07 to 17:22, N33).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] ai-tables-stay-readable
A table keeps a readable width for each column (a description never below about 230dp)
and scrolls sideways with a fade at its edge; no column is squeezed to a few letters. In
"In the code" the place sits on its own line and its reason under it at full width
(rule 95; F62).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ai-brief-is-data
A brief or tour page arrives as a plain `{type, props}` tree and is drawn natively from
the kit; it is data, never executed. A component the app does not know is not drawn
(architecture, The brief).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ask-never-needs-analyze
Ask opens the chat and the reader can ask at once, on a pull request that was never
analysed (rule 62).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] ask-replies-are-plain
The AI's reply is plain text with no box, fill or shadow; only the person's own message
is a bubble, in the accent. There is never a bubble with dots in it ("I don't want that
ever"), and "Clear" is not a word on the screen: a new-chat button sits at the top right
(rule 99; F67, F68, F69).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ask-streams-and-cites
Ask streams its thinking and its answer as they are written, with no jump when the saved
reply takes over. Under each answer, source chips (the files it read and the places it
names) scroll to their place, and two or three follow-up questions tap to send (rule 99;
F70).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ask-opens-without-the-keyboard
The chat opens at its tall height at once with no keyboard, and may still be dragged
down to half; tapping the field brings the keyboard ("it goes into this text mode
immediately" was jarring, rule 77). Tavi changed the opening height from the normal one
to the tall one (recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 11:37 to 11:47, N25).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ask-send-needs-text
Send does nothing until its field has text (rule 84; F65). With nothing typed the button is
the earlier chats of the pull request instead, by Tavi's choice (L36); it is a grey Send
only where there are no earlier chats to offer.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ai-analyze-is-one-action
Analysing a pull request is one action with three outputs (a summary, a note per file and
a tour), called Analyze, never "Write tour" (rule 19).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ai-presets-start-the-run
On the Analyze options page, tapping Quick, Standard or Deep starts the analysis at once
("pretty awesome"); choosing a model only saves it (rule 89; F34).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ai-file-notes-show-on-rows
The AI's note for each file shows on its file row, in two lines at most, at once (rules
19 and 102; F44).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] ask-progress-like-the-tour
Ask's work on an answer looks like the Tour's progress: the shimmering verb and time over
the steps with their icons, the same component, with no orb or bars of its own under the
steps ("the thinking does not look the same", recording 15 Oct 15:37, 16:09 to 16:14; L31).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ask-loader-in-the-button
While an answer is on its way the turning orb sits in the field's button, where Send was,
and a tap on it stops the answer ("that should just be where the button is", recording
15 Oct 15:37, 16:28 to 16:35; L33).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] ask-scroll-is-the-readers
An answer being written MUST NOT scroll the reader back down once they have scrolled up;
the sheet follows the end only while they are at it, and again when they let go at the
end or tap the round scroll-to-the-end button that shows once they are away from it. Only
the reader's own drags let go of the end. A question sent goes to the top of the sheet
with its answer written under it, and the sheet does not follow the answer down, as
shadcn's Conversation does (recording 15 Oct 15:37, 16:14 to 16:23; L32; strengthened by
Tavi, recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 11:48 to 12:47, N26).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ask-answers-draw-like-tours
Answers in Ask MAY use the tour's forms (tables, call trees, file trees, pseudocode, flows,
diagrams, real-language code) and the sheet draws them as the Tour does (recording 15 Oct
15:37, 16:45 to 16:58; L34).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] ask-new-chat-is-instant
New chat empties the page at once, and an empty chat, the first or a new one, offers its
starting questions as the same rows that follow an answer, in a card ("it took a while to
load ... that's not how the other one looks", recording 15 Oct 15:37, 16:58 to 17:12; L35).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ask-history-of-chats
A pull request keeps its earlier chats. With nothing typed, the field's button opens them
on a sheet built from the shared searchable list, newest first, each its first question,
when and how many questions; a tap brings one back and the open chat takes its place in the
list (Tavi's idea, recording 15 Oct 15:37, 17:19 to 17:48; L36).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] ask-field-floats-over-the-chat
Ask's field floats over the conversation, which runs on under it and dissolves into the
paper as the Tour's page does under its Ask bar; there is no solid band of paper under
the field ("a white band under the input", recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 13:06 to 13:16,
N27).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] tour-sheet-holds-tour-things
On the Tour, ⋯ opens the tour's own sheet: Model with Effort as its own row under it
(rule 142), Analyze options, then Regenerate tour, Ask about this tour and Switch to the
diff, and last a row on to the pull request's actions. It opens in the frame of the tap,
drawn from what the phone holds ("took far too long to open", recording of 16 Oct 12:10,
10:37 to 10:43, N22; "on the Tour, ⋯ should hold tour things", 10:49 to 11:24, N23).
